.\" ###### Setup ############################################################
.Dd November 15, 2026
.Dt getrelativepath 1
.Os getrelativepath
.\" ###### Name #############################################################
.Sh NAME
.Nm getrelativepath
.Nd Relative Path Computation Tool
.\" ###### Synopsis #########################################################
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm getrelativepath
.Ar from_path to_path
.Nm getrelativepath
.Op Fl h | Fl \-help
.Nm getrelativepath
.Op Fl v | Fl \-version
.\" ###### Description ######################################################
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm getrelativepath
computes and prints the relative path from
.Ar from_path
to
.Ar to_path .
Symbolic links as well as
.Pa .
and
.Pa ..
path components are resolved against the filesystem, and the resulting relative path is written to standard output.
.Pp
.\" ###### Arguments ########################################################
.Sh ARGUMENTS
The following arguments and options may be provided:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Ar from_path
The starting (base) path.
.It Ar to_path
The target (destination) path.
.It Fl h | Fl \-help
Prints command\-line help.
.It Fl v | Fl \-version
Prints program version.
.El
.\" ###### Exit status ######################################################
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The
.Nm
tool exits with 0 on success, and >0 in case of an error.
.\" ###### Examples #########################################################
.Sh EXAMPLES
Compute the relative path to an ancestor directory:
.Bd -literal
getrelativepath ~/src/netperfmeter/src/tests ~/src/netperfmeter/
.Ed
.Pp
Output:
.Bd -literal
\&../..
.Ed
.Pp
Compute the relative path to a sibling directory:
.Bd -literal
getrelativepath ~/src/netperfmeter/src/tests ~/src/netperfmeter/examples
.Ed
.Pp
Output:
.Bd -literal
\&../../examples
.Ed
.Pp
Compute the relative path to a subdirectory:
.Bd -literal
getrelativepath ~/src/netperfmeter ~/src/netperfmeter/src/tests
.Ed
.Pp
Output:
.Bd -literal
src/tests
.Ed
